                    {
                        "sense_id": "44bfb588-ebe5-37a6-b27a-ed9400712359",
                        "entry_id": "6904dd93-ec8a-3ba4-b1ff-4cbd8e98b84c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Making a hissing sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a3e551f-ad39-4af7-a06b-c3d36652bb62",
                                "sense_id": "44bfb588-ebe5-37a6-b27a-ed9400712359",
                                "text": "Each is very inexpensive ($60 per two-pack for the Midland, $100 a pair for the Audiovox), and feels it. Each is also tiny, no bigger than a bar of Ivory. Both are far hissier than their more expensive rivals, and don't have as much range (more on this in a moment)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b20619ae-ba81-3c8a-b3b0-47f3f75c2655",
                        "entry_id": "6904dd93-ec8a-3ba4-b1ff-4cbd8e98b84c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Childish or petulant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e364f600-f709-4cff-b771-d65f18c6e857",
                                "sense_id": "b20619ae-ba81-3c8a-b3b0-47f3f75c2655",
                                "text": "Viewers were aghast. . . . As co-host Regis Philbin flinched, Gifford launched into a teary, it's-not-my-fault, TV hissy fit: \"You can say I'm ugly, you can say I'm not talented, but when you say I don't care about children, how dare you!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04b4c143-3d27-4e35-8459-64b1f17a919f",
                                "sense_id": "b20619ae-ba81-3c8a-b3b0-47f3f75c2655",
                                "text": "Midwestern-bred and still wholesome despite his exposure to New York’s hissiest, Sam remains the play’s anchor."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
